V2.1.5-beta (2026-11-17)
Item 4(b) checks the multiplicities against the structure: every letter counts (strict reading), the large
couplings (J >= 6 Hz) of every signal must be given by protons that can stand at its shift, a signal with fewer
large couplings must be wide enough for them (the width test), and every constant must fit the coupling range of
those protons. Item 1 checks that the integrals fit the sets of equivalent protons. A 19F/31P description
without J leaves an H-X partner unverifiable. A description without any coupling constant and with an "m" is
"NOT CHECKED by items 3, 4(a) and 6" instead of "NO INCONSISTENCY FOUND".
A beta until its accuracy is measured on the test articles of the second data set (OSF Update 3).
Not the version that gives the results of the survey: those come from the frozen version of 18 October 2026
(measuring scripts of 17 October); version 1.1 is its code cleanup with identical output (see CHANGELOG.md).
